- !<TypeScriptAssetData/aecf4a3a-f468-4437-923d-0b41bab70b15>
  SvgIcon: ""
  SetupScript:
    code: ""
  Description: |-
    POLYGONAL BUTTON - SCRIPTING API EXAMPLES
    You can cast this component from another script to access its properties. Example setup in another script: @input myButton: ScriptComponent;
    
    onAwake() \{ this.buttonAPI = this.myButton as any; \}
    
    --- 1. OPACITY --- Property: opacity (number between 0.0 and 1.0) Use Case: You want a button to slowly fade in when a user looks at a specific object, or fade out when a menu is closed. Example: // Inside an update event for a fade-out animation this.buttonAPI.opacity = MathUtils.lerp(this.buttonAPI.opacity, 0.0, getDeltaTime() * 5.0);
    
    --- 2. ANIMATION TYPE --- Property: getAnimationType / setAnimationType (number: 0=Scale, 1=Position Z, 2=Both, 3=None) Use Case: Your button usually just changes color when clicked (3), but during a specific "tutorial" phase of your app, you want it to physically pop out on the Z-axis (1) so the user knows they need to press it. Example: this.buttonAPI.setAnimationType = 1;
    
    --- 3. POP DISTANCE --- Property: getPopDistance / setPopDistance (number in cm) Use Case: You have a button that sits flush against a wall. When the user selects a "magnify" tool in your app, you want the button's hover-pop distance to increase significantly so it sticks out further from the wall. Example: this.buttonAPI.setPopDistance = 5.0;
    
    --- 4. DEFAULT BASE COLOR --- Property: getDefaultColor / setDefaultColor (vec4 RGBA) Use Case: You have a "Save" button. When the user has unsaved changes, you want the button to turn bright red. Once they save, you want it to revert back to grey. This changes the idle color without breaking the hover/click highlight colors. Example: // Turn button red this.buttonAPI.setDefaultColor = new vec4(1.0, 0.0, 0.0, 1.0);
    
    --- 5. DEFAULT BORDER COLOR --- Property: getBorderColor / setBorderColor (vec4 RGBA) Use Case: Similar to the base color, but applied to the border. You might want the border to pulse green when a process is complete. Example: this.buttonAPI.setBorderColor = new vec4(0.0, 1.0, 0.0, 1.0);
    
    --- 6. POLYGON SCALE --- Method: setPolygonScale(vec2) Use Case: You are building a health bar UI. Instead of stretching the 3D SceneObject transform (which might distort the border width), you use polygonScale to dynamically shrink the internal geometry along the X-axis based on the player's health. Example: // Shrink button width to 50% this.buttonAPI.setPolygonScale(new vec2(0.5, 1.0));
